    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="fc-overview">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="fc-overview" data-i18n="ovTitle">01 · Overview</h2>
      <div class="chapter-body pair">
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovProbT">The problem</h3>
          <p data-i18n="fcProb">
            In 2018, the number of people investing in public service exams in Brazil was growing about 40% a
            year, and abstention could reach 60%, as many candidates felt they had no chance against hundreds of
            thousands of applicants. Our interviews showed candidates struggled to keep a study routine, assess
            what they knew, and understand the exam notice.
          </p>
          <p class="t-caption src-note" data-i18n="fcProbSrc">
            Sources: Estúdio Correio (2018); a prep-course school director interviewed by UOL (2018).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovGoalT">The goal</h3>
          <p data-i18n="fcGoal">
            How might we help exam candidates organize their studies and assess their knowledge before the exam?
            We took this question through the full UX process during a two-week intensive course at Mergo.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="fc-research">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="fc-research" data-i18n="reTitle">02 · Research</h2>
      <figure class="chapter-body quote">
        <blockquote data-i18n="fcQuote">
          “With two kids and working until 11pm, it’s hard to find time to study, right?!”
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption data-i18n="fcQuoteCap">
          Graziela, 33, nurse, interviewee (translated from Portuguese)
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="insights five">
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR1t">No time</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR1">Lack of time to study was the most common finding.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR2t">No routine</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR2">Creating and keeping a daily study routine was the hardest for most people.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR3t">Weak spots first</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR3">In the little time they had, candidates focused on their hardest subjects.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR4t">Past exams as practice</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR4">To assess themselves, they used mock tests built from past exam questions.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR5t">Skipping the exam notice</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR5">
            Many interviewees didn’t read the exam notice, partly because they couldn’t even find it.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

